# GENEALOGIX Repository Code Owners
#
# These owners are AUTO-REQUESTED on matching PRs. They are ALSO a merge gate:
# the "Main Protection" ruleset sets require_code_owner_review = true (see #258),
# so a PR cannot merge without an approving review from a listed owner of every
# changed path. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins and a matched owner set REPLACES
# earlier matches; the catch-all stays FIRST and any narrower rule must list
# EVERY owner it wants, not just the extra one.
#
# Learn more: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Both maintainers on the default so EITHER is auto-requested on any PR --
# deliberate cross-review / bus-factor insurance for a 2-person team. This
# covers go-glx/, glx/, specification/, docs/, website/, .github/, ci-tools/,
# scripts/, tools/, public/, LICENSES/, and root manifests. Do NOT add
# per-directory rules that just re-list these two owners (no-ops + drift).
* @noahbjohnson @isaacschepp

# Add narrower rules below ONLY when they CHANGE the owner set (a different/
# additional owner). A same-owner line changes nothing. See #258 before
# adding a security tier on .github/workflows/ -- a CODEOWNERS line there is
# meaningful only after a distinct owner (third maintainer / org team) exists
# to escalate to; with the current 2-person roster every path resolves to the
# same two owners, so a narrower rule would only risk sole-owner deadlock.
